TI  - Establishing mouse attention deficit hyperactivity            disorder model involves calculating pregnancy mouse            pregnancy period through female bolt, vaginal smear and            abdomen ultrasound, intraperitoneal injection of            isilolamineketone, and overhead cross maze
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - Method for establishing a mouse attention                deficit hyperactivity disorder model, involves (a)                mating male and female mice cage, (b) calculating                the pregnancy period of the mouse through the                female bolt, the vaginal smear and the abdomen                ultrasound, (c) injecting isilolamineketone, (d)                performing cross maze, and (e) performing an open                field test on the child mouse to evaluate the                behavior of child mouse attention and hyperactivity                disorders to obtain a model of mouse                attention-and-hyperactivity disorder.
                    USE - The method is useful for establishing mouse                attention deficit hyperactivity disorder model. The                method can be used in the technical field of animal                model construction.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method is capable of completely simulating                actual neutron generation mouse attention deficit                hyperactivity disorder behavior, and is simple and                easy, and has high success rate.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a female mouse in the                presence of a vaginal plug.
